but you  know that's that's how you go up a  mountain in this case anyway that's the  that's the lift I'm gonna refer to it in  as a poem if it's in the future I guess  because it really is specifically a lift  by the manufacturer palma but anyway i  wanted to add a bit of detailing to this  and a small fence that protects the the  people on the lift from the people  outside the lift who might crash into  them  you never know it's not actually that  important and you don't always see it in  real life but it's something I figured  was worth adding and also before I  finish that I wanted to add a small  cabin just for whoever's operating the  lifts and I'm not sure what it's like  for these kind of lifts I've never  actually been on a poem I lift myself  all of the similar lifts that I've been  on were by the manufacturer Doble Meyer  which is the same manufacturer for the  gondolas and chair lifts that we have in  the game at least judging by what they  look like but yeah I don't know if this  manufacturer usually adds they're  they're sort of cabins there they're  operator Hut's  on the top or the bottom of the lift but  in this case I just decided to add it up  here because I felt it would look a bit  better and for the style of this  building I'm basically creating the same  kingpost roofs but then on a smaller  scale so it's very similar to the  restaurant building but just a tiny  version of it's basically once again I  kind of feel I didn't really need to go  that far but at this point I just had  too much fun with these things I'm not  sure if you can expect me to go back to  this method of doing roofs I'm probably  gonna scale it down a little bit but  it's good to have it in mind and  know what the actual structure of a roof  is like because it can really help to  make your roofs look better more  realistic and more detailed so for  anyone who's interested I'm also going  to link honestly whenever a kind of  resource I can find down in the  description about these kinds of roofs  so you can learn and teach yourself  about how to build the cool wooden roofs  anyway that is just about it for this  episode so I'd like to thank you guys  for watching and I hope to see you in  the next one I have no idea what I'm  gonna be doing but it'll probably be  something skiing related bye guys  [Music]  you
 

